  Copy to <repo-root>/CLAUDE.local.md

  THIS FILE IS NOT COMMITTED. Add it to .gitignore (see gitignore-snippet.txt).
  It loads alongside CLAUDE.md and is treated exactly the same way - the only
  difference is that it is yours.

  This is the correct home for everything the committed CLAUDE.md must not
  contain: drive letters, absolute checkout paths, machine quirks, personal
  preferences for this one repo.

  WORKTREE CAVEAT: because this file is gitignored, it does NOT exist in a new
  git worktree created by `claude --worktree`. If you use worktrees, put the
  content in a home-directory file and import it here instead:

      @~/.claude/<repo-name>-local.md

  A project-level import that resolves outside the working directory triggers a
  one-time approval dialog. Accept it once and it stops asking.
  (You can also list this file in .worktreeinclude at the repo root, which tells
  Claude Code to copy matching gitignored files into each new worktree.)
-->

# Local notes - <repo-name>

## Where my checkouts live

<!-- The absolute paths that must never be committed. -->
- This repo: `<H:\Repos\this-repo>`
- `<other-repo-name>`: `<I:\RepositoryMetadata\other-repo>`
- Scratch / working area: `<I:\Scratch\this-repo>`

Sibling access is granted via `.claude/settings.local.json`
(`permissions.additionalDirectories`) or `claude --add-dir <path>` at launch.

